      "text": "Hello from Vietnam! 🇻🇳 The historical continuity in this script is amazing. Learning that the oldest continuous synagogue in the Americas still keeps sand on the floor to remember the days of the Inquisition when they had to muffle their footsteps [09:05] is one of the most poetic architectural details I've ever heard. It’s the ultimate irony that the Spanish called it a \"useless island,\" yet it became a safe haven for so many cultures to invent Papiamentu and thrive [06:13]. Incredible research! 🏛❤",
